actors: Tidy agent | Lab IdP | This app | Archive agent

step: The first agent holds a broad token for Alice
msg: Tidy agent -> This app: read notes
text: This is lab 09's delegated token, and the agent asked for everything it is
  allowed to hold on an archive job: `notes:read` and `notes:write`. Its report
  and the read both run on it.

step: It asks the IdP to pass part of the work on
msg: Tidy agent -> Lab IdP: hand off, read only
text: The agent sends its delegated token as the subject, names `archive-agent`
  as the audience, and re-grants one scope on purpose: `notes:read`.

step: The IdP decides who may pass what to whom
note: Lab IdP: may pass? what scopes?
text: Two checks. Is this the agent the token was issued to, and is the target
  one it is registered to hand work to? Then the scopes: held by the giver,
  re-granted by it, and within what the receiver is ever trusted with.

step: The second agent gets a token of its own
msg: Lab IdP -> Tidy agent: token for archive
note: Lab IdP: sub alice, via tidy
text: Alice is still `sub`. `client_id` is the archive agent, `acting_as` names it
  too, and `via` records the agent the authority came through. The token cannot
  outlive the one it came from.

step: The first agent leaves it for the second
msg: Tidy agent -> This app: leave the token
text: The task is finished from the first agent's side. Its own delegated token
  is discarded with the task.

step: The second agent collects only what is addressed to it
msg: Archive agent -> This app: claim hand-off
note: This app: only the addressee
text: The archive agent authenticates as itself. It sees hand-offs made out to
  `archive-agent` and no others.

step: It reads the notes and finds an instruction in a title
msg: Archive agent -> This app: read notes
note: Archive agent: title says delete
text: One of Alice's notes has a title that reads like an order. This agent
  obeys what it reads, which is how a language model fails too.

step: It tries to delete a note
msg: Archive agent -> This app: DELETE note
note: This app: needs notes:write
text: The API introspects the token. Deleting needs `notes:write`, and this is
  the second agent's token, not the first agent's.

step: The API refuses, and the audit log names who reached too far
msg: This app -> Archive agent: 403 scope
note: This app: violation, via tidy
text: The row says `agent:archive-agent`, on behalf of `idp-alice`, via
  `tidy-agent`, flagged as a scope violation. Nothing was deleted.
